IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-seizure.l4 -- ss 164, 164.1, 164.2 and 164.3: warrants of seizure of illicit material, the order to delete material from a computer system, forfeiture after conviction and relief from it.
-- Powers of a judge or court ("may") whose gate is an "if" answer NOTHING when the gate fails (the ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1)); the court's "shall" duties answer JUST FALSE when their "if" fails (limit (2)).
-- A period the text fixes in its own words ("within seven days", "within thirty days", "at least fifteen days", "within 48 hours") is JUST FALSE outside the period (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05).
-- The time unit of every regulative rule below is a day, except s 164.1(5.1), whose unit is an hour.

§ `s 164 Warrant of seizure`

-- (8) the definitions come first because the rest reads them. "court means (a) in the Province of Quebec, ..." is a "means": the court named for another province is JUST FALSE (the keel's reading of "superior court of criminal jurisdiction", fork F12).
DECLARE `s 164(8) court named` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(8)(a) the Court of Quebec`
    `s 164(8)(a) the municipal court of Montreal`
    `s 164(8)(a) the municipal court of Quebec`
    `s 164(8)(a.1) the Superior Court of Justice`
    `s 164(8)(b) the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    `s 164(8)(d) the Supreme Court`
    `s 164(8)(e) the Nunavut Court of Justice`
    `s 164(8) another court`

-- src:3283 | Definitions
-- src:3284 | (8) In this section,
-- src:3285 | advertisement for conversion therapy [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 18]
-- src:3286 | advertisement of sexual services [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 18]
-- src:3287 | court means
-- src:3288 | (a) in the Province of Quebec, the Court of Quebec, the municipal court of Montreal and the municipal court of Quebec,
-- src:3289 | (a.1) in the Province of Ontario, the Superior Court of Justice,
-- src:3290 | (b) in the Provinces of New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Court of Queen’s Bench,
-- src:3291 | (c) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 5]
-- src:3292 | (c.1) [Repealed, 1992, c. 51, s. 34]
-- src:3293 | (d) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador, in Yukon and in the Northwest Territories, the Supreme Court, and
-- src:3294 | (e) in Nunavut, the Nunavut Court of Justice; (tribunal)
-- src:3295 | crime comic [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 12]
-- src:3296 | illicit material means
-- src:3297 | (a) any visual representation that is or is likely to be mistaken for a photographic, film, video or other visual recording of a person committing bestiality, as defined in subsection 160(7),
-- src:3298 | (b) a visual recording, as defined in subsection 162(2), that is made as described in subsection 162(1),
-- src:3299 | (c) an intimate image, as defined in subsection 162.1(2), in relation to which an offence was committed under section 162.1,
-- src:3300 | (d) a publication that is obscene, within the meaning of subsection 163(8),
-- src:3301 | (e) child sexual abuse and exploitation material, as defined in subsection 163.1(1),
-- src:3302 | (f) any material — including a photographic, film, video, audio or other recording, made by any means, a visual representation or any written material — that is used to advertise sexual services contrary to section 286.4, or
-- src:3303 | (g) any material — including a photographic, film, video, audio or other recording, made by any means, a visual representation or any written material — that is used to promote or advertise conversion therapy contrary to section 320.103; (matériel illicite)
-- src:3304 | intimate image [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 18]
-- src:3305 | judge means a judge of a court. (juge)
-- src:3306 | voyeuristic recording [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 18]
@ref Criminal Code s 164(8) court (src:3283-3306)
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory`
      court IS A `s 164(8) court named`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(8) court` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `s 164(8)(a) the Court of Quebec` THEN IF province EQUALS Quebec THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "court means (a) in the Province of Quebec, the Court of Quebec, the municipal court of Montreal and the municipal court of Quebec"
    WHEN `s 164(8)(a) the municipal court of Montreal` THEN IF province EQUALS Quebec THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the Province of Quebec, the Court of Quebec, the municipal court of Montreal and the municipal court of Quebec"
    WHEN `s 164(8)(a) the municipal court of Quebec` THEN IF province EQUALS Quebec THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the Province of Quebec, the Court of Quebec, the municipal court of Montreal and the municipal court of Quebec"
    WHEN `s 164(8)(a.1) the Superior Court of Justice` THEN IF province EQUALS Ontario THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a.1) in the Province of Ontario, the Superior Court of Justice"
    WHEN `s 164(8)(b) the Court of Queen’s Bench` THEN
        IF province EQUALS `New Brunswick` OR province EQUALS Manitoba OR province EQUALS Saskatchewan OR province EQUALS Alberta THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the Provinces of New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Court of Queen’s Bench"
    WHEN `s 164(8)(d) the Supreme Court` THEN
        IF    province EQUALS `Nova Scotia` OR province EQUALS `British Columbia` OR province EQUALS `Prince Edward Island`
           OR province EQUALS `Newfoundland and Labrador` OR province EQUALS Yukon OR province EQUALS `Northwest Territories`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island and Newfoundland and Labrador, in Yukon and in the Northwest Territories, the Supreme Court"
    WHEN `s 164(8)(e) the Nunavut Court of Justice` THEN IF province EQUALS Nunavut THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) in Nunavut, the Nunavut Court of Justice"
    WHEN `s 164(8) another court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "court means"

@ref Criminal Code s 164(8) judge (src:3305)
GIVEN `s 164(8) court` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of that court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(8) judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 164(8) court` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "judge means a judge of a court", and the court was not answered
        IF `s 164(8) court` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person is a judge of that court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judge means a judge of a court"

-- illicit material means (a) to (g). Five of the seven limbs read definitions of this Part (answers of `s 160(7) bestiality`, `s 162(2) visual recording`, `s 162.1(2) intimate image`, `s 163(8)` and `s 163.1(1)`),
-- and two read offences in other parts (s 286.4, s 320.103): each limb is an input, a MAYBE BOOLEAN, and a limb that is NOT COVERED is not turned into "not illicit material".
@ref Criminal Code s 164(8) illicit material (src:3296-3303)
GIVEN `(a) it is a visual representation that is or is likely to be mistaken for a recording of a person committing bestiality, as defined in subsection 160(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `(b) it is a visual recording, as defined in subsection 162(2), that is made as described in subsection 162(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `(c) it is an intimate image, as defined in subsection 162.1(2), in relation to which an offence was committed under section 162.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `(d) it is a publication that is obscene, within the meaning of subsection 163(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `(e) it is child sexual abuse and exploitation material, as defined in subsection 163.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 286.4: (f) it is material used to advertise sexual services contrary to section 286.4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 320.103: (g) it is material used to promote or advertise conversion therapy contrary to section 320.103` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(8) illicit material` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    `(a) it is a visual representation that is or is likely to be mistaken for a recording of a person committing bestiality, as defined in subsection 160(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `(b) it is a visual recording, as defined in subsection 162(2), that is made as described in subsection 162(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `(c) it is an intimate image, as defined in subsection 162.1(2), in relation to which an offence was committed under section 162.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `(d) it is a publication that is obscene, within the meaning of subsection 163(8)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `(e) it is child sexual abuse and exploitation material, as defined in subsection 163.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 286.4: (f) it is material used to advertise sexual services contrary to section 286.4` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 320.103: (g) it is material used to promote or advertise conversion therapy contrary to section 320.103` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    `(a) it is a visual representation that is or is likely to be mistaken for a recording of a person committing bestiality, as defined in subsection 160(7)` EQUALS NOTHING
           OR `(b) it is a visual recording, as defined in subsection 162(2), that is made as described in subsection 162(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
           OR `(c) it is an intimate image, as defined in subsection 162.1(2), in relation to which an offence was committed under section 162.1` EQUALS NOTHING
           OR `(d) it is a publication that is obscene, within the meaning of subsection 163(8)` EQUALS NOTHING
           OR `(e) it is child sexual abuse and exploitation material, as defined in subsection 163.1(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
           OR `s 286.4: (f) it is material used to advertise sexual services contrary to section 286.4` EQUALS NOTHING
           OR `s 320.103: (g) it is material used to promote or advertise conversion therapy contrary to section 320.103` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb of the definition turns on another definition or another part's offence, and its answer was not given
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "illicit material means"

-- (1) "A judge may issue a warrant authorizing seizure ... if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that (a) ... (b)": a power with an "if" gate, so NOTHING when the gate fails.
-- Paragraph (b) adds "in the case of material alleged to be illicit material described in any of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition ..., are so kept for sale or distribution".
-- src:3263 | Warrant of seizure
-- src:3264 | 164 (1) A judge may issue a warrant authorizing seizure of copies of any material — including a recording, publication or written material, or representation — if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that
-- src:3265 | (a) the material is illicit material; and
-- src:3266 | (b) copies of the material are kept in premises within the jurisdiction of the court and, in the case of material alleged to be illicit material described in any of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition of that term in subsection (8), are so kept for sale or distribution.
@ref Criminal Code s 164(1) (src:3263-3266)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the material is illicit material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that copies of the material are kept in premises within the jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material is alleged to be illicit material described in any of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition of that term in subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that copies of the material are so kept for sale or distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(1) a judge may issue a warrant authorizing seizure of copies of the material` MEANS
    IF    `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the material is illicit material`
      AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that copies of the material are kept in premises within the jurisdiction of the court`
      AND (   `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that copies of the material are so kept for sale or distribution`
           OR (NOT `the material is alleged to be illicit material described in any of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition of that term in subsection (8)`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge may issue a warrant authorizing seizure of copies of any material ... if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that (a) the material is illicit material; and (b) copies of the material are kept in premises within the jurisdiction of the court"

-- The parties of the regulative rules of ss 164 to 164.3 (the core's `Party` has no constructor for the occupier, the custodian of a computer system or a person who claims an interest in a thing forfeited: NEEDS-CORE.md).
DECLARE `ss 164 to 164.3 party` IS ONE OF
    `ss 164 to 164.3 the judge`
    `ss 164 to 164.3 the custodian of the computer system`
    `ss 164 to 164.3 a person who claims an interest in the thing forfeited`
    `ss 164 to 164.3 the applicant for relief from forfeiture`

DECLARE `s 164(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(2) issue a summons to the occupier of the premises requiring them to appear before the court and show cause why the seized thing should not be forfeited to His Majesty`

-- (2) "Within seven days of the day on which the warrant is issued, the judge shall issue a summons to the occupier".
-- src:3267 | Summons to occupier
-- src:3268 | (2) Within seven days of the day on which the warrant is issued, the judge shall issue a summons to the occupier of the premises requiring them to appear before the court and show cause why the seized thing should not be forfeited to His Majesty.
@ref Criminal Code s 164(2) (src:3267-3268)
GIVEN `the number of days from the day on which the warrant was issued to the day on which the judge issued the summons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(2) the judge issued the summons within seven days of the day on which the warrant was issued` MEANS
    IF `the number of days from the day on which the warrant was issued to the day on which the judge issued the summons` AT LEAST 0 AND `the number of days from the day on which the warrant was issued to the day on which the judge issued the summons` AT MOST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within seven days of the day on which the warrant is issued, the judge shall issue a summons to the occupier of the premises"

@ref Criminal Code s 164(2) (src:3268)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 164 to 164.3 party` `s 164(2) act`
`s 164(2) the judge's duty to issue the summons` MEANS
    PARTY `ss 164 to 164.3 the judge`
    MUST `s 164(2) issue a summons to the occupier of the premises requiring them to appear before the court and show cause why the seized thing should not be forfeited to His Majesty`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `ss 164 to 164.3 the judge` BECAUSE "the judge did not issue the summons to the occupier within seven days of the day on which the warrant was issued"

-- (3) "The owner and the maker of the seized thing that is alleged to be illicit material may appear and be represented in the proceedings to oppose the making of an order for the forfeiture of the thing."
-- src:3269 | Owner and maker may appear
-- src:3270 | (3) The owner and the maker of the seized thing that is alleged to be illicit material may appear and be represented in the proceedings to oppose the making of an order for the forfeiture of the thing.
@ref Criminal Code s 164(3) (src:3269-3270)
GIVEN `the person is the owner of the seized thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the maker of the seized thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seized thing is alleged to be illicit material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(3) the person may appear and be represented in the proceedings to oppose the forfeiture` MEANS
    IF (`the person is the owner of the seized thing` OR `the person is the maker of the seized thing`) AND `the seized thing is alleged to be illicit material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The owner and the maker of the seized thing that is alleged to be illicit material may appear and be represented in the proceedings"

-- (4) "If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the seized thing is illicit material, it may make an order declaring the thing to be forfeited": a power, an "if" gate.
-- src:3271 | Order of forfeiture
-- src:3272 | (4) If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the seized thing is illicit material, it may make an order declaring the thing to be forfeited to His Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place, for disposal as the Attorney General may direct.
@ref Criminal Code s 164(4) (src:3271-3272)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the seized thing is illicit material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(4) the court may make an order declaring the thing forfeited to His Majesty in right of the province` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the seized thing is illicit material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the seized thing is illicit material, it may make an order declaring the thing to be forfeited to His Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place"

-- (5) "If the court is not satisfied that the seized thing is illicit material, it shall order that the thing be restored to the person from whom it was seized without delay after the time for final appeal has expired."
-- src:3273 | Restoration
-- src:3274 | (5) If the court is not satisfied that the seized thing is illicit material, it shall order that the thing be restored to the person from whom it was seized without delay after the time for final appeal has expired.
@ref Criminal Code s 164(5) (src:3273-3274)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the seized thing is illicit material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(5) the court must order the thing restored to the person from whom it was seized` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is satisfied that the seized thing is illicit material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is not satisfied that the seized thing is illicit material, it shall order that the thing be restored to the person from whom it was seized"

@ref Criminal Code s 164(5) (src:3274)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the seized thing is illicit material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time for final appeal has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(5) the thing is to be restored now` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the court is satisfied that the seized thing is illicit material`) AND `the time for final appeal has expired`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall order that the thing be restored to the person from whom it was seized without delay after the time for final appeal has expired"

DECLARE `s 164(6) the ground of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `s 164(6)(a) a question of law alone`
    `s 164(6)(b) a question of fact alone`
    `s 164(6)(c) a question of mixed law and fact`
    `s 164(6) another ground`

-- (6) "An appeal lies from an order made under subsection (4) or (5) by any person who appeared in the proceedings (a) ... (b) ... (c) ...".
-- src:3275 | Appeal
-- src:3276 | (6) An appeal lies from an order made under subsection (4) or (5) by any person who appeared in the proceedings
-- src:3277 | (a) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of law alone,
-- src:3278 | (b) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of fact alone, or
-- src:3279 | (c) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of mixed law and fact,
-- src:3280 | as if it were an appeal against conviction or against a judgment or verdict of acquittal, as the case may be, on a question of law alone under Part XXI and sections 673 to 696 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref Criminal Code s 164(6) (src:3275-3280)
GIVEN `the order is made under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appeared in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of appeal` IS A `s 164(6) the ground of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(6) an appeal lies from the order` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under subsection (4) or (5)` AND `the person appeared in the proceedings` AND NOT (`the ground of appeal` EQUALS `s 164(6) another ground`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal lies from an order made under subsection (4) or (5) by any person who appeared in the proceedings (a) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of law alone, (b) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of fact alone, or (c) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of mixed law and fact"

-- (7) "no proceedings shall be instituted or continued in that province under subsection 160(3.1) or section 162, 162.1, 163, 163.1, 286.4 or 320.103 with respect to those or other copies of the same material without the consent of the Attorney General."
-- src:3281 | Consent
-- src:3282 | (7) If an order is made under this section by a judge in a province with respect to one or more copies of any material, no proceedings shall be instituted or continued in that province under subsection 160(3.1) or section 162, 162.1, 163, 163.1, 286.4 or 320.103 with respect to those or other copies of the same material without the consent of the Attorney General.
@ref Criminal Code s 164(7) (src:3281-3282)
GIVEN `an order has been made under this section by a judge in the province with respect to one or more copies of the material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are under a provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the proceedings are with respect to those or other copies of the same material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164(7) no proceedings shall be instituted or continued without the consent of the Attorney General: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `an order has been made under this section by a judge in the province with respect to one or more copies of the material`
               AND `the proceedings are with respect to those or other copies of the same material`
               AND (   `ss 150 to 182 the provision is the subsection` `the proceedings are under a provision` 160 "(3.1)"
                    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the proceedings are under a provision` 162
                    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the proceedings are under a provision` 162.1
                    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the proceedings are under a provision` 163
                    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the proceedings are under a provision` 163.1
                    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the proceedings are under a provision` 286.4
                    OR `ss 150 to 182 the provision is in the section` `the proceedings are under a provision` 320.103))
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an order is made under this section by a judge in a province with respect to one or more copies of any material, no proceedings shall be instituted or continued in that province under subsection 160(3.1) or section 162, 162.1, 163, 163.1, 286.4 or 320.103 with respect to those or other copies of the same material"
        IF `the Attorney General has consented`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the consent of the Attorney General"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 164.1 Warrant of seizure: material on computer system`

DECLARE `s 164.1(1) what the judge may order the custodian to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 164.1(1)(a) give an electronic copy of the material to the court`
    `s 164.1(1)(b) ensure that the material is no longer stored on and made available through the computer system`
    `s 164.1(1)(c) provide the information necessary to identify and locate the person who posted the material`
    `s 164.1(1) something else`

-- src:3307 | Warrant of seizure — material on computer system
-- src:3308 | 164.1 (1) If a judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that material, consisting of illicit material or of computer data that makes illicit material available, is stored on and made available through a computer system that is within the jurisdiction of the court, the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to
-- src:3309 | (a) give an electronic copy of the material to the court;
-- src:3310 | (b) ensure that the material is no longer stored on and made available through the computer system; and
-- src:3311 | (c) provide the information necessary to identify and locate the person who posted the material.
@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(1) (src:3307-3311)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that material consisting of illicit material, or of computer data that makes illicit material available, is stored on and made available through a computer system that is within the jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the judge orders` IS A `s 164.1(1) what the judge may order the custodian to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(1) the judge may order the custodian of the computer system` MEANS
    IF    `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that material consisting of illicit material, or of computer data that makes illicit material available, is stored on and made available through a computer system that is within the jurisdiction of the court`
      AND NOT (`what the judge orders` EQUALS `s 164.1(1) something else`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that material, consisting of illicit material or of computer data that makes illicit material available, is stored on and made available through a computer system that is within the jurisdiction of the court, the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to (a) give an electronic copy of the material to the court; (b) ensure that the material is no longer stored on and made available through the computer system; and (c) provide the information necessary to identify and locate the person who posted the material"

-- (2) "Within a reasonable time after receiving the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c), the judge shall cause notice to be given to the person who posted the material ...". The period is "a reasonable time": an open-textured judgment, left to the court; the function asks only whether the duty has arisen.
-- src:3312 | Notice to person who posted the material
-- src:3313 | (2) Within a reasonable time after receiving the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c), the judge shall cause notice to be given to the person who posted the material, giving that person the opportunity to appear and be represented before the court, and show cause why the material should not be deleted. If the person cannot be identified or located or does not reside in Canada, the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to post the text of the notice at the location where the material was previously stored and made available, until the time set for the appearance.
@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(2) (src:3312-3313)
GIVEN `the judge has received the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(2) the judge must cause notice to be given to the person who posted the material` MEANS
    IF `the judge has received the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within a reasonable time after receiving the information referred to in paragraph (1)(c), the judge shall cause notice to be given"

@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(2) (src:3313)
GIVEN `the person who posted the material cannot be identified or located, or does not reside in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(2) the judge may order the custodian to post the text of the notice` MEANS
    IF `the person who posted the material cannot be identified or located, or does not reside in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the person cannot be identified or located or does not reside in Canada, the judge may order the custodian of the computer system to post the text of the notice"

-- src:3314 | Person who posted the material may appear
-- src:3315 | (3) The person who posted the material may appear and be represented in the proceedings in order to oppose the making of an order under subsection (5).
@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(3) (src:3314-3315)
GIVEN `the person posted the material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(3) the person may appear and be represented in the proceedings to oppose the order` MEANS
    IF `the person posted the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The person who posted the material may appear and be represented in the proceedings"

-- src:3316 | Non-appearance
-- src:3317 | (4) If the person who posted the material does not appear for the proceedings, the court may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the proceedings in the absence of the person as fully and effectually as if the person had appeared.
@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(4) (src:3316-3317)
GIVEN `the person who posted the material does not appear for the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(4) the court may proceed ex parte` MEANS
    IF `the person who posted the material does not appear for the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the person who posted the material does not appear for the proceedings, the court may proceed ex parte"

-- src:3318 | Order
-- src:3319 | (5) If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is illicit material or computer data that makes illicit material available, it may order the custodian of the computer system to delete the material.
@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(5) (src:3318-3319)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is illicit material or computer data that makes illicit material available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(5) the court may order the custodian to delete the material` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is illicit material or computer data that makes illicit material available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is illicit material or computer data that makes illicit material available, it may order the custodian of the computer system to delete the material"

-- (5.1) "If the illicit material is an intimate image ... the court must order the custodian ... to delete the material within 48 hours after the order is made."
-- src:3320 | Order — intimate image
-- src:3321 | (5.1) If the illicit material is an intimate image, as defined in subsection 162.1(2), in relation to which an offence was committed under section 162.1, the court must order the custodian of the computer system to delete the material within 48 hours after the order is made.
@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(5.1) (src:3320-3321)
GIVEN `s 162.1(2) intimate image: the illicit material is an intimate image in relation to which an offence was committed under section 162.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(5.1) the court must order the custodian to delete the material within 48 hours` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 162.1(2) intimate image: the illicit material is an intimate image in relation to which an offence was committed under section 162.1`
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the illicit material is an intimate image, as defined in subsection 162.1(2), in relation to which an offence was committed under section 162.1, the court must order the custodian of the computer system to delete the material"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the material is an intimate image depends on `s 162.1(2)` and was not answered

@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(5.1) (src:3321)
GIVEN `the number of hours from the making of the order to the deletion of the material` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(5.1) the material was deleted within 48 hours after the order was made` MEANS
    IF `the number of hours from the making of the order to the deletion of the material` AT LEAST 0 AND `the number of hours from the making of the order to the deletion of the material` AT MOST 48
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to delete the material within 48 hours after the order is made"

DECLARE `s 164.1(5.1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 164.1(5.1) delete the material`

@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(5.1) (src:3321)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 164 to 164.3 party` `s 164.1(5.1) act`
`s 164.1(5.1) the custodian's duty to delete the intimate image` MEANS
    PARTY `ss 164 to 164.3 the custodian of the computer system`
    MUST `s 164.1(5.1) delete the material`
    WITHIN 48
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `ss 164 to 164.3 the custodian of the computer system` BECAUSE "the custodian did not delete the intimate image within 48 hours after the order was made"

-- (6) "When the court makes the order for the deletion of the material, it may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court's possession": a power whose gate is "When": JUST FALSE under ruling (b) (fork F9).
-- src:3322 | Destruction of copy
-- src:3323 | (6) When the court makes the order for the deletion of the material, it may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court’s possession.
