GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(6) the court may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court's possession` MEANS
    IF `the court makes the order for the deletion of the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the court makes the order for the deletion of the material, it may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court’s possession"

-- src:3324 | Return of material
-- src:3325 | (7) If the court is not satisfied that the material is illicit material or computer data that makes illicit material available, the court shall order that the electronic copy be returned to the custodian of the computer system and terminate the order made under paragraph (1)(b).
@ref Criminal Code s 164.1(7) (src:3324-3325)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the material is illicit material or computer data that makes illicit material available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 164.1(7) the court must order the electronic copy returned and terminate the order made under paragraph (1)(b)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is satisfied that the material is illicit material or computer data that makes illicit material available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is not satisfied that the material is illicit material or computer data that makes illicit material available, the court shall order that the electronic copy be returned to the custodian of the computer system and terminate the order made under paragraph (1)(b)"

-- src:3326 | Other provisions to apply
-- src:3327 | (8) Subsections 164(6) and (7) apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to this section.
